course: dictionary
lesson: 14085
title: A formal word for medicine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Medicament is a stiff, formal word for medicine. It means a substance used to treat an illness or an injury, such as a tablet, cream or syrup. «The nurse read the label on the medicament before giving it to Sam.» Here the label and the nurse tell you that medicament is a kind of medicine.
explain: Most people just say "medicine", and a doctor or parent would say it too. You will mostly meet medicament on packets, in leaflets, in old books and in exam texts. «Keep this medicament out of reach of young children.» The careful, serious tone of that sentence is a clue that the writing is official.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in an easy word. «Keep this medicine out of reach of young children» still makes perfect sense, so medicament means medicine. In French, médicament is the everyday word, which is why translators sometimes use it.
fact: Medicament means a medicine: a substance used to treat an illness or injury.
fact: Medicament is a noun. You can say «a medicament» or «medicaments».
fact: Medicament is a formal word. Most people say "medicine" in everyday speech.
fact: «Medicament» is often found on packets, in leaflets and in old books.
fact: Context clue: «Keep this medicament out of reach of young children» sounds official, so the word is formal.
exercise: «The doctor gave Sam a medicament for his sore throat.» What does medicament mean? | A game played in the school hall | *A medicine used to treat an illness | A type of hat worn by doctors
exercise: The leaflet says «Keep this medicament out of reach of children.» Which everyday word means the same? | Garden | Puzzle | *Medicine | Sandwich
exercise: The leaflet said «Store the medicament in a cool, dry place.» What kind of writing is this? | A shopping list | A text message from a friend | A comic strip | *An official or formal leaflet
test: «She took her medicament with a glass of water.» What is her medicament? | *Medicine, a tablet or syrup to treat illness | A kind of cake | A pair of shoes | A school bag
test: Which sentence uses medicament correctly? | We played medicament in the park | The dog ate the medicament for breakfast | The sky was a bright medicament blue | *The pharmacist checked the medicament on the shelf
exam: Which word is the best everyday replacement for medicament in «The medicament will help your cough»? | Vegetable | *Medicine | Holiday | Blanket
